eans that  they're trying to get to mars but they  don't have time to make a ship of their  own and still be competitive with nasa  and the soviets who are both planning on  launching their mission in four years he  wants to buy the hotel and put these new  engines on it so that he can get into  the race in the process of trying to  make the deal he tells karen an  inspiring speech about his father that  explains why he's interested in the  first place and it seems like we can  probably take him at his word at this  point in the story and when all is said  and done she gets a great deal and he  gets a spaceship at jsc molly learns  through a memo that the higher-ups are  trying to gain more influence over her  office she goes looking for margot who  still isn't back from her trip and we  watch her complain to emma then she  decides to make a move she goes back to  her office calls in danielle tells her  she won't be the commander of mars 96  and it's clear that she's doing this to  strike back against margot she's doing  it when she's not there she's doing it  even though she told her that they would  talk whenever she got back and she knows  this will cause problems but the way  things are currently set up she still  has the ultimate authority and decides  to use it she laid out her reasons in  the premiere of why she thought that ed  was the better choice and she tells  danny the same thing she obviously  doesn't agree but doesn't have a problem  with running ed's backup crew molly goes  to tell him the good news and he's  beside himself he can't believe it and  he is really pumped up we catch up with  karen who's clearing out her office at  polaris and danny stops by while he's  there to pick up tracy's astronaut pin  from sans office she has to ask him why  he played the song at the reception and  he lies at first saying it was his  wife's idea and then leaves but turns  right back around and comes back in to  tell her that he lied he makes a play  telling her that he can't put it behind  him even after all these years and she  shuts it down in a way that doesn't  leave any room for misinterpretation she  even adds a little slap in there which  is a nice touch we get the idea that  there's a long history of this sort of  thing that when he was drinking he was  showing up to her house drunk and that  she thought that he had gotten over it  that he moved past it when he got sober  one thing that i thought was interesting  is that he brings up ed and it's clear  that he really doesn't like them  together it seems like him being worried  that they might get back together is a  part of what's happening right now she  doesn't want to have anything to do with  it and she tells him that he needs to go  home to his wife and he does eventually  leave  at their home ellen and larry are  discussing her idea of having john  mccain as her running mate and he's  against it he stresses that she needs to  get someone that's different that will  appeal to the base especially someone  who will bring in the evangelicals and  he does mention that at this point she's  behind bill clinton in the polls later  she'll have a meeting with this new  character governor bragg where she does  bring him on board but the real twist in  this scene is that ellen and larry have  a child it's a big surprise and they  have this nice interaction where they  seem like one big happy family at the  office danny and ed continue their  friendly rivalry you can tell that she's  devastated not to get the command but  she does back her friend up and  congratulate him for getting the mission  and we see them share a moment he goes  to call kelly and offers her a spot on  his crew we learned that he's ending his  marriage with yvonne and that this isn't  the first divorce that he's had after  karen i'm guessing it's the second but  the way she says it there could be more  i guess i thought it stood out that one  of the reasons that margot favored danny  was her interest 