ecide to hire him on her way  out deb stops her to offer her a job  doing whatever she wants basically she'd  be recruiting people and at first she  isn't interested he picks up on the fact  that it's because of what happened with  the hotel and he gives her an inspiring  pep talk that brings her around and she  agrees to come on board back at nasa  margot tells danny that elena worked out  the glitch in the nerva engine they  talked crew wishlist and the idea that  ed was going to bring kelly comes up  before she tells margo she wants danny  stevens as her right seat and this makes  me really question the writer's decision  to name both of these characters danny  before they can discuss that nori comes  in and tells them to turn on the tv deb  is holding a press conference where he  announces that karen's now working for  helios then he explains their plan to  repurpose polaris by adding their  methane engines to take it to mars they  renamed it phoenix and they announced  that ed will be the commander of their  mission which will be launching in the  next window a full two years before nasa  and the soviets plan to launch their  missions in the end ed got what he  wanted and when you see him on that  stage you have to wonder if that might  not go to his head there's gonna be a  giant competition here he wants to get  there first because he's been living  with this regret that he had a chance to  be the first person on the moon but he  decided to follow his mission instead he  was just awful to a long time friend  with a totally incorrect and out of line  statement and danny is playing for the  home team so you can bet that nasa is  going to do everything in their power to  try to get her there first the soviets  might have real problems getting their  engine together two years sooner  everything we've seen so far seems to  indicate that they were gonna have  trouble getting it together for 96 and  that means that margot might end up in a  bad situation because of 